From local/main-external-wait-tmpdir Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zbai29 <zbai29@wisc.edu>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] External-wait finish deferral and hidden system send

Keep the original caller subscription alive across externally resumed work,
and let controllers resume with `paseo send --system` so the prompt uses the
hidden <paseo-system> path instead of a user-message bubble.

Rebased onto getpaseo/paseo v0.5.0-beta.2 (ccd991b3e). Does not include
machine-local TMPDIR defaults.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
diff --git a/docs/agent-lifecycle.md b/docs/agent-lifecycle.md
index db9762cbe..0851a8062 100644
--- a/docs/agent-lifecycle.md
+++ b/docs/agent-lifecycle.md
@@ -61,6 +61,28 @@ Runtime ownership is resolved from explicit workspace ID and caller context, nev
 Users can also detach an existing subagent from the subagents track. Detach is deliberately a manual lifecycle gesture, not an agent-facing MCP tool. It removes the parent and open-tab lifecycle labels: it does not stop, archive, move, or restart the agent. The agent keeps its current `cwd` and `workspaceId`, leaves the former parent's track, and behaves like a root agent for tab close, workspace activity, and future parent archive.
 
 `notifyOnFinish` defaults to `true` for agent-scoped creation and background prompt follow-ups because most delegated work needs to report back to the creating agent. Set it to `false` only for truly fire-and-forget agents or prompts.
+
+### External waits
+
+A child can defer its existing finish notification while work continues outside its provider runtime.
+Set the reserved `paseo.external-wait-id` label to a non-empty wait identifier before the turn
+becomes idle. The caller's finish subscription stays active, but that idle edge does not notify the
+caller.
+
+One identifier may represent a group of external operations. For an `each` controller, keep the same
+label while sending intermediate completion prompts; every resumed turn may become idle without
+notifying the caller. Clear the label before sending the group's final completion prompt. The final
+resumed turn's next idle edge notifies the original caller unless the child registered another
+external wait. An `all` controller simply keeps the label until every operation is terminal and then
+sends one final prompt.
+
+The label marks an external controller's ownership; Paseo does not interpret the identifier or poll
+the external system, group membership, or completion strategy. The controller must serialize its
+state transitions and completion prompts. Errors and permission requests still notify the caller
+immediately. Clearing the label while the child is idle does not itself complete the delegated task.
+External controllers should resume the child with `paseo send --system`; this uses the same hidden
+system-context path as child-to-parent finish notifications instead of adding a user-message bubble
+to the timeline.
 Permission requests are notification checkpoints, not the end of that subscription. The caller is notified again after a permission response when the child finishes, errors, or requests another permission.
 The permission notification includes the normalized request plus the child and request IDs, so the caller can inspect it and respond without fetching agent status.
 A watched child that closes before its finish event also notifies the caller so delegated work cannot disappear silently during archive or workspace teardown.
